1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,646
Why does a man pull away

2
00:00:01,646 --> 00:00:03,247
from the woman he loves…

3
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:05,997
right when his life is at its hardest?

4
00:00:06,297 --> 00:00:08,296
From the outside, it's confusing.

5
00:00:08,296 --> 00:00:09,504
If he loves her…

6
00:00:09,504 --> 00:00:11,254
why would he leave?

7
00:00:11,554 --> 00:00:13,199
Because what a man feels…

8
00:00:13,199 --> 00:00:14,712
and how he handles it…

9
00:00:14,712 --> 00:00:17,028
are not always the same thing.

10
00:00:17,328 --> 00:00:18,680
When everything inside him

11
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,979
starts to collapse…

12
00:00:19,979 --> 00:00:21,632
when he feels lost, drained,

13
00:00:21,632 --> 00:00:23,422
and out of control…

14
00:00:23,722 --> 00:00:24,897
he's not thinking about

15
00:00:24,897 --> 00:00:26,371
how to keep her close.

16
00:00:26,371 --> 00:00:27,937
He's thinking about how not to

17
00:00:27,937 --> 00:00:29,903
drag her down with him.

18
00:00:30,204 --> 00:00:31,597
His logic becomes simple:

19
00:00:31,597 --> 00:00:32,718
If I'm on fire…

20
00:00:32,718 --> 00:00:34,542
I have to protect the ones I love

21
00:00:34,542 --> 00:00:36,118
from the flames.

22
00:00:36,418 --> 00:00:37,463
His life has become

23
00:00:37,463 --> 00:00:38,545
a burning ship.

24
00:00:38,545 --> 00:00:40,320
So the first thing he does…

25
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:41,981
is push her away.

26
00:00:42,281 --> 00:00:43,710
And he stays on deck.

27
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,098
Because it's his ship.

28
00:00:45,098 --> 00:00:46,317
His responsibility.

29
00:00:46,317 --> 00:00:47,656
He either saves it…

30
00:00:47,656 --> 00:00:49,319
or sinks with it.

31
00:00:49,618 --> 00:00:51,743
The problem is, in these moments…

32
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:53,260
he forgets how to love.

33
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:54,298
He goes quiet.

34
00:00:54,298 --> 00:00:55,615
Closed off.

35
00:00:55,914 --> 00:00:58,088
Not because his feelings disappeared…

36
00:00:58,088 --> 00:00:59,307
but because he believes

37
00:00:59,307 --> 00:01:01,047
this is something he has to face

38
00:01:01,047 --> 00:01:02,102
alone.

39
00:01:02,402 --> 00:01:03,622
And that's exactly where

40
00:01:03,622 --> 00:01:05,375
men lose everything.

41
00:01:05,674 --> 00:01:06,766
So many relationships

42
00:01:06,766 --> 00:01:07,849
end right here.

43
00:01:07,849 --> 00:01:10,204
Not because the love was gone…

44
00:01:10,504 --> 00:01:12,203
but because she saw his distance

45
00:01:12,203 --> 00:01:13,197
as rejection…

46
00:01:13,197 --> 00:01:14,501
and he saw her closeness

47
00:01:14,501 --> 00:01:15,861
as pressure.

48
00:01:16,161 --> 00:01:17,554
If each of them understood

49
00:01:17,554 --> 00:01:19,592
what the other was going through…

50
00:01:19,592 --> 00:01:22,040
they would have made it together.

51
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,765
So if he pulls away…

52
00:01:23,765 --> 00:01:24,848
don't chase him.

53
00:01:24,848 --> 00:01:26,108
And don't disappear.

54
00:01:26,108 --> 00:01:27,194
Just let him know:

55
00:01:27,194 --> 00:01:29,075
I'm not going anywhere.

56
00:01:29,375 --> 00:01:31,205
Because the right kind of closeness

57
00:01:31,205 --> 00:01:32,548
doesn't add pressure…

58
00:01:32,548 --> 00:01:34,691
it makes the storm smaller.

59
00:01:34,991 --> 00:01:36,079
Send this to someone

60
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:37,508
who needs to hear it.

61
00:01:37,508 --> 00:01:39,302
And follow for more.
